To change the background color of an Adaptive Card in a Bot Framework bot using C#, you can set the background color property of the card's styling. Adaptive Cards support a `backgroundColor` property that can be used to set the background color of the card.

Here's how you can do it:

1. Create an Adaptive Card JSON with the `backgroundColor` property.
2. Use the `Activity` object to send the card to the user.

Example:

```csharp
using Microsoft.Bot.Builder;
using Microsoft.Bot.Schema;
using System;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

namespace AdaptiveCardBot
{
    public class MyBot : ActivityHandler
    {
        protected override async Task OnMessageActivityAsync(ITurnContext<IMessageActivity> turnContext, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
        {
            // Create an Adaptive Card
            var card = new AdaptiveCard("1.0")
            {
                BackgroundColor = "#FF0000", // Set the background color to red
                Body = new[]
                {
                    new TextBlock
                    {
                        Text = "Hello, this is an Adaptive Card with a red background!",
                        Size = TextSize.Large,
                        Weight = TextWeight.Bolder
                    }
                }
            };

            // Create an Attachment with the card
            var attachment = new Attachment
            {
                ContentType = "application/vnd.microsoft.card.adaptive",
                Content = card
            };

            // Create an activity with the card
            var activity = MessageFactory.Text("Here is your card:");
            activity.Attachments.Add(attachment);

            // Send the activity
            await turnContext.SendActivityAsync(activity, cancellationToken);
        }
    }
}
```

In this example, the `BackgroundColor` property of the `AdaptiveCard` is set to `#FF0000`, which is the hexadecimal color code for red. You can change this to any valid color code you prefer.

Note: Make sure you have the necessary NuGet packages installed, such as `Microsoft.Bot.Builder` and `Microsoft.Bot.Schema`. Also, the `AdaptiveCard` class is part of the `Microsoft.Bot.Schema` namespace.

